The conformance cases of the flash1-dev matching engine benchmark
(https://github.com/flash1-dev/matching-engine-benchmark, commit
424e4e5649652febb5b0c4c80859d74c4654131e), one pair of files per case:

  CASE.bin  the case's messages as the workload file the benchmark reads,
            written by write_bin and EDGE_CASES of its
            scripts/conformance_check.py (scripts/harness.sh setup)
  CASE.txt  the canonical report stream of the case, as the benchmark's
            --write-canonical-output writes it; Liquibook, CppTrader and
            geseq/orderbook each produced exactly this file
            (scripts/harness.sh cases)

The cases are taken from the benchmark under its license:

